Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:37:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] e-ink: display off between the sleep screen's minute updates

The composer of the HiBreak Pro has no doze mode, so SurfaceFlinger runs
the always-on display (DOZE and DOZE_SUSPEND) with the display fully on.
The display driver then holds cmdq_wake_lock and the SoC never suspends:
measured 42 mAh an hour asleep, 99.9 % of the time awake.

An e-ink panel keeps its picture with the display off. With the e-ink
sleep screen, DozeScreenState now turns the display off once the sleep
screen is on the panel (debug.sysui.eink_sleep.off_ms, 3000); the doze
time tick turns it on for the new minute and off again after the update
(tick_ms, 1500). debug.sysui.eink_sleep.screen_off=0 keeps the display on.
